Construct the known component $3\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OP} &=3\,(1, -1)=(3, -3). \\
\overrightarrow{PC} &=(-1, 0).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](images/9a/9a193e20dd46765efa19a097c486108c52549134abe3c55757196ed9045bbcd7.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(-2, 0)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Horizontal scale} &=\frac{-1}{-2}=\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{PC}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OP}+\overrightarrow{PC} \\
&=3\mathbf{a}+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=3\mathbf{a}+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{1}{2}$.
